{
  "reason": "Select only model_design because dropout is model-owned and preprocessing, training, and evaluation are frozen. Repeated dropout across eight blocks may disrupt sparse histories averaging approximately 10.7 training interactions per user, although validation HR@10 of 0.665 at epoch 15/35 does not establish excessive regularization. Historical successes support retaining the current gated branches, learned residual scales, and modest weight decay; unsuccessful dilation and positional ablations favor isolating the proposed dropout reduction.",
  "module": ["model_design"],
  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": null,
    "model_design": "Perform one regularization ablation: change DROPOUT_RATE from 0.2 to 0.1 and the NextItNetModel constructor default to dropout_rate: float = 0.1, retaining the existing dropout_rate propagation so embedding dropout and both residual-branch dropout applications use the same rate to preserve more sequential evidence. Preserve the current position-free causal NextItNet exactly, including eight independent blocks with dilations [1,2,4,8,1,2,4,8], gated local/dilated branches, learned per-channel residual scales initialized to 0.1, normalization, GELU, initialization, padding masks, tied item embeddings, and candidate-scoring logic. Keep MAXLEN=128, HIDDEN_UNITS=64, NUM_BLOCKS=8, KERNEL_SIZE=3, LR=0.001, WEIGHT_DECAY=0.00001, and BATCH_SIZE=128 unchanged, preserving all existing variable names and constructor, forward, encode_sequence, and score_candidates interfaces except the intended dropout default change. Retain exactly the three permitted imports, eight numeric constants, and two classes with methods only; leave preprocessing, splits, validation candidates, training seed 2024, validation sampling seed 42, BPR loss, Adam, clipping, 35 epochs, training negatives, checkpoint selection, evaluation, and checkpoint/candidate-score submission under the unchanged frozen host, adding no model-side training, evaluation, printing, file/network access, or CSV generation. Allocate one candidate within the total 44-slot budget and compare its host-selected validation HR@10 against 0.665 on the same 200 users with 99 negatives each, treating 0.675–0.685 as an unmeasured target of two to four additional hits and using no test metric or prediction ensemble.",
    "training_evaluation": null
  }
}
